      "description": "Watch OFI vs Hoffenheim highlights and goals from UEFA Europa League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 17, 2026. The stage was set for a compelling UEFA Europa League clash on September 17, 2026, as OFI hosted Hoffenheim . With both sides eager to make a statement in the group stage, the match promised a blend of tactical discipline and European intensity under the floodlights. First Half Breakthrough The contest began with a physical edge, as the referee was called into action early to manage the tempers. Hoffenheim's Vladimir Coufal received the first booking of the match in the 23rd minute, reflecting the pressure the visitors were under. The breakthrough arrived exactly at the half-hour mark. Kenan Kodro turned provider, delivering a sharp pass to Aitor Cantalapiedra , who made no mistake in finding the target. His clinical finish put OFI ahead and shifted the momentum firmly in favor of the home side. Despite Hoffenheim's attempts to find an immediate response, the OFI defense remained resolute. The first half concluded after three minutes of stoppage time with the hosts holding a slender but deserved lead. Tactical Adjustments and Rising Tension The second half saw Hoffenheim introduce Koki Machida for Albian Hajdari in an attempt to stabilize their backline. However, the game remained a feisty affair. Between the 53rd and 64th minutes, four yellow cards were brandished, with Nathan De Cat , Thanasis Androutsos , Koki Machida , and goal-scorer Aitor Cantalapiedra all entering the official's book. Managers from both sides looked to their benches for inspiration, with Andrej Kramaric and Bambase Conte entering for the visitors, while OFI brought on Giorgios Kanellopoulos to shore up the midfield. As the clock ticked down, the tension in the stadium grew, with the German side pushing forward and leaving spaces behind for the Greek outfit to exploit. Late Drama Seals the Result The decisive blow came in the 84th minute, orchestrated by two players who had recently entered the fray. Borja Gonzalez , who replaced Lorenzo Dickmann in the 80th minute, proved to be a tactical masterstroke. Gonzalez provided a brilliant assist for Giorgios Kanellopoulos , who fired home to double the lead. The late goal effectively ended Hoffenheim's hopes of a comeback. After five minutes of additional time, the referee blew the final whistle, confirming a significant victory for OFI . The result highlighted the importance of squad depth, as the substitutes played a pivotal role in securing the points on a memorable European night."
